  "body": "Parallel 3D Finish now accepts a direction angle in the Passes tab and through MCP. The angle runs counterclockwise from the positive X axis of the active work coordinates. It accepts values from 0 degrees up to 360 degrees, with 360 excluded. A project without the field uses 0 degrees and keeps its original path and generation stamp.\n\nThe generator projects the existing model and stock bounds onto the requested raster directions. It evaluates the cutter contact and limits in their existing coordinates. The operation edit command records the new angle in the undo history. Other finish patterns keep their paths when the saved angle changes.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n**Parallel Passes before** (`68d645261`)\n\n![Parallel Passes before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/56dbd20fbcd463c112086d3af21336f653954ab5/3426/3426-parallel-before.png)\n\n**Parallel Passes after** (`832434c59`)\n\n![Parallel Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/56dbd20fbcd463c112086d3af21336f653954ab5/3426/3426-parallel-after.png)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `parallel_direction_uses_mcp_history_and_survives_project_round_trip` failed on parent `68d645261` when MCP refused 45 degrees as an unknown field. On the feature branch, the MCP suite passed all 24 tests. It covers add, edit, undo, redo and old project files.\n- At 0 and 90 degrees, the flat-top part has at least four separate interior tracks and more than 35 mm of measured cutting feed. The tests check the direction of the actual segments.\n- `parallel_angles_cut_the_clipped_roof_and_pass_verification` passed on the asymmetric sloped part at all cardinal angles and at 45 degrees. The 45-degree case also passed with 30 degrees of work-coordinate yaw. The checks cover clipping, tip contact, and the app gouge verifier.\n- The 33 CL golden tests passed. Zero degrees also matched the original generator moves. Invalid input was refused and other finishing patterns kept their paths.\n- At `832434c59`, the complete UI library passed 1,429 tests with seven ignored. The named Direction angle control also passed separately. Strict Clippy passed for all app, motion, and UI targets.\n- The touched-binary gate passed on this head. The app ran 581 passing tests across 10 targets with seven ignored. Motion ran 627 passing tests across nine targets with 44 ignored. The 200-step broad quick plan was a dry run. The first release batch passed 47 tests across seven selected heavy steps. Two additional optimized binaries passed all four direction tests and 13 area-control tests. The heavy results include 33 finishing tests, one gap-link test, the Q02 finish fixture, and stock verification. All 242 selected release-mode execution steps have now completed. In total they recorded 105 passing ignored tests and four registered expected failures. Of the 242 steps, 205 had no ignored cases to run. The separate aggregate compile-only step was omitted. The two additional optimized binaries above are outside these counts.\n\nNo physical machine run was performed.\n\n## Review gates on head 832434c59 (AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\", #3556)\n\n- Base of the quick plan: `68d64526122eaf4f32fddc5b4f0b545decbbc020` (the merge base of this PR with `origin/main`). The gates ran on the PR head as it is, with no merge of main.\n- Pinning tests: `mcp_finish3d_direction::parallel_direction_uses_mcp_history_and_survives_project_round_trip` (in `app suites: mcp`) and `parallel_angles_cut_the_clipped_roof_and_pass_verification` (in `app suites: finish3d_direction`) passed in the quick plan below.\n- `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4 cargo xtask gate quick --base 68d645261`: 200 steps, 0 failed. 3,700 tests passed, 0 failed, 78 ignored.\n- `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` of `camcraft-app` (`cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: <binary>\"`; the quick plan does not select them): 3 steps, 0 failed. 39 tests passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored.\n- `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4 cargo xtask gate light`: 3 steps (1 release build, 2 light steps), 0 failed. 2 tests passed, 0 failed.\n\nChangelog: Set the cutting direction for Parallel 3D Finish from the Passes tab or through MCP.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2377\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
